<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><nav class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> &rsaquo; <a href="/services">Services</a> &rsaquo; <span>Anxiety</span></nav><span class="eyebrow-white">Condition</span><h1>Anxiety Disorder Treatment</h1><p>Targeted medication management and evidence-based therapy for generalized anxiety, panic disorder, social anxiety, and related conditions. Helping you reclaim your daily life.</p></div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="two-col"><div><span class="eyebrow">About Anxiety</span><h2>More Than Just Worry</h2><p>Anxiety disorders are the most common mental health conditions, yet they are also among the most treatable. While occasional anxiety is a normal part of life, anxiety disorders involve persistent, excessive worry or fear that significantly interferes with daily activities, relationships, work, and overall quality of life.</p><p>Anxiety can take many forms: generalized anxiety disorder (GAD), panic disorder, social anxiety disorder, specific phobias, and more. Each requires a specific diagnostic approach and tailored treatment plan. Many people with anxiety also have co-occurring depression, ADHD, or OCD.</p><p>Matthew Mauro conducts thorough evaluations to accurately diagnose the type of anxiety you&rsquo;re experiencing and create a personalized treatment plan that may include medication management, cognitive behavioral therapy, or a combination of approaches.</p><a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top:var(--sp-4)">Schedule an Appointment &#8594;</a></div>
<div><div style="background:var(--teal-light);border-radius:var(--radius-xl);padding:var(--sp-8);border:1px solid var(--border)"><span class="eyebrow">Common Signs</span><h3 style="margin-bottom:var(--sp-6)">Anxiety Symptoms to Watch For</h3><div class="condition-signs"><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Persistent, excessive worry most days</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Difficulty controlling worry or fear</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Physical symptoms: racing heart, sweating</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Avoidance of feared situations</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Panic attacks (sudden intense fear)</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Fear of social situations or judgment</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Sleep disturbances and irritability</p></div><div class="sign-item"><div class="sign-check">&#10003;</div><p>Difficulty concentrating; mind going blank</p></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="section section-light"><div class="container" style="max-width:860px"><div class="section-header center"><span class="eyebrow">Treatment</span><h2>Evidence-Based Anxiety Treatment</h2></div><div class="treatment-list"><div class="treatment-item"><div class="treatment-icon">&#128065;</div><div><h4>Comprehensive Diagnostic Evaluation</h4><p>Accurate diagnosis of the specific type of anxiety disorder is essential to effective treatment. Matthew conducts thorough evaluations to distinguish anxiety types and identify any co-occurring conditions.</p></div></div><div class="treatment-item"><div class="treatment-icon">&#128138;</div><div><h4>Medication Management</h4><p>SSRIs, SNRIs, buspirone, and other evidence-based medications can significantly reduce anxiety symptoms. Matthew carefully selects, monitors, and adjusts medications to find the best fit for you.</p></div></div><div class="treatment-item"><div class="treatment-icon">&#129504;</div><div><h4>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)</h4><p>CBT is one of the most effective treatments for anxiety disorders. It helps identify and reframe anxiety-provoking thought patterns and teaches practical skills for managing anxiety in real life.</p></div></div><div class="treatment-item"><div class="treatment-icon">&#128200;</div><div><h4>Ongoing Monitoring</h4><p>Regular follow-up appointments to track progress, adjust the treatment plan, and ensure you are moving toward the relief and quality of life you deserve.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

<section class="cta-section"><div class="container"><h2>Relief Is Possible</h2><p>You do not have to live with debilitating anxiety. Reach out today &mdash; we can help.</p><div class="cta-phone"><a href="tel:4437987707">(443) 798-7707</a></div><div class="cta-actions"><a href="/contact" class="btn btn-white btn-lg">Schedule Appointment</a><a href="/services" class="btn btn-outline-white btn-lg">All Services</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
